---
import Band from '../components/Band.astro'
import PageHeader from '../components/PageHeader.astro'
import Row from '../components/Row.astro'
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'

// §6.3: do not add a "delegate your vote" row. Delegation is recognised by the
// Charter but the governance platform doesn't support it yet — it becomes a
// fifth row here once it does, with no other change required.
---

<BaseLayout
	title="Participate"
	description="How to propose, vote, stand for election, or challenge a decision for breaking a rule."
>
	<Band>
		<PageHeader question="How do I take part?" heading="How to take part">
			<p class="mt-5 max-w-[52ch] text-[1.0625rem] text-[var(--color-muted)]">
				Anyone holding XRD can take part. No registration, no minimum holding, and no approval
				from any DAO body.
			</p>
		</PageHeader>

		<div class="mt-10 border-t border-[var(--color-rule)]">
			<Row
				key="Propose"
				lead="Open to any token holder."
				href="https://vote.radixdao.org"
				linkText="Start a proposal"
			>
				No minimum holding, no prior registration, and no approval step. It moves through draft
				discussion, a temperature check, then a binding vote.
			</Row>
			<Row
				key="Vote"
				lead="Voting power is your XRD put in action, wherever in the network you have deployed it."
				href="https://vote.radixdao.org/about/voting-power"
				linkText="What counts as voting power"
			>
				One XRD is one vote. Validator LSUs and LSULP count for the XRD underneath them, and
				eligible liquidity positions on Ociswap, CaviarNine and DefiPlaza count for the XRD, LSU or
				LSULP held inside the position — never the other side of the pair. It is measured against a
				published allowlist, at a snapshot taken when each vote opens.
			</Row>
			<Row
				key="Stand"
				lead="Council seats and Working Group Steward roles are elected."
				href="/govern/"
				linkText="Read the elections policy"
			>
				Terms are time-bound and renewable by vote. Any token holder may stand.
			</Row>
			<Row
				key="Challenge"
				lead="A published result can be challenged for breaking a rule. There is no veto."
				href="/contact/"
				linkText="How to file a challenge"
			>
				For 48 hours after a result is published, any holder of at least 0.1% of voting power can
				file a compliance challenge: the claim that the decision breaks a specific rule, not that
				it is unwise. The Accountability Council decides whether a rule was broken — if none was,
				the decision stands. Filings are published to the record exactly as received.
			</Row>
		</div>
	</Band>
</BaseLayout>
